		<category><![CDATA[Anthony Kiedis]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Arsenio Hall]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Dick Tracy]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[gay]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Rosie O'Donnell]]></category>

		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://drownedmadonna.com/?p=928</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[<p>Famed talk-show host Arsenio Hall talks about his interviews with Madonna. Arsenio admits that a few of the interviews with [...]</p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/arsenio-hall-loves-madonna/20140618">Arsenio Hall loves Madonna</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna new album news unapologetic</a>.</p>
]]></description>
				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Famed talk-show host <strong>Arsenio Hall</strong> talks about his interviews with <strong>Madonna</strong>. Arsenio admits that a few of the interviews with <strong>Madonna</strong> were kinda &#8220;tense&#8221;, but he is very enthusiastic of them all. &#8220;She was always good,&#8221; says <strong>Arsenio</strong>.</p>
<p>His favourite past interview with <strong>Madonna</strong> was the time she brought Rosie O&#8217;Donnell in to speak about A League of Their Own.</p>
<p>Arsenio is also proud of the time Madonna was at the 1000th anniversary of his show performing with Red Hot Chili Peppers&#8217; Anthony Kiedis. &#8220;We ended that show with her [<strong>Madonna</strong>] on my neck running around,&#8221; tells <strong>Arsenio</strong>.</p>
<blockquote class="pixcode  pixcode--testimonial  testimonial testimonial--small-text">
    <div class="testimonial__content">
<p>She was always good to the show and the good thing about <strong>Madonna</strong> is there&#8217;s always that little bit of tension, with you don&#8217;t know if this is gonna go alright, and you don&#8217;t know if she likes the host, whether she is going to cooperate.</p>
</div>

    
        
            <div class="testimonial__author-name">Arsenio Hall</div>
        
        
        
    </blockquote>

<p>The host also tells that after the show, he and <strong>Madonna</strong> went to a Laker game, with Rosie O&#8217;Donnell as his date and Charles Barkley as her date.</p>
<p><strong>Arsenio</strong> also speaks about the interview with <strong>Madonna</strong> to promote Dick Tracy, when they started hurling gay rumors at one another.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/arsenio-hall-loves-madonna/20140618">Arsenio Hall loves Madonna</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna new album news unapologetic</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
